        "### (f) Reflection: What information is lost during compression?\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QXz1il6RXbjT"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Solution:** Spatial resolution and fine details are lost during the pooling steps of the encoder. The reconstructed image looks blurry because the decoder has to guess the lost details from the compressed latent representation (a bottleneck).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "q7zMa6LXXbjT"
      },
      "source": [
        "### (g) Add a simple skip connection\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "twkoT6exXbjT"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class UNetConcept(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.encoder = SimpleEncoder()\n",
        "        self.decoder = SimpleDecoder()\n",
        "        self.final_conv = nn.Conv2d(2, 1, 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        # x is 28x28x1\n",
        "        latent = self.encoder(x)\n",
        "        reconstructed = self.decoder(latent)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Skip connection: concatenate original input with reconstruction\n",
        "        combined = torch.cat([x, reconstructed], dim=1)\n",
        "        out = self.final_conv(combined)\n",
        "\n",
        "        return torch.sigmoid(out)\n",
        "\n",
        "unet = UNetConcept()\n",
        "unet_out = unet(img.unsqueeze(0))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
